WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.196 --> 00:00:16.118
friar and the short friar didn't know what to do.

2
00:00:16.138 --> 00:00:20.901
This strange gigantic friar in a short robe wanted to travel with them!

3
00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:26.025
"You should stay here at the inn," the tall friar said to Little John.

4
00:00:26.045 --> 00:00:33.021
"Yes! We don't want to wear you out," added the short friar in his nicest voice.

5
00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:34.901
His name was Thomas.

6
00:00:34.921 --> 00:00:39.282
"We'll ride our horses, but you'll be walking.

7
00:00:39.963 --> 00:00:42.083
It will be exhausting for you."

8
00:00:42.103 --> 00:00:47.425
"Oh, don't worry about me," Little John said cheerfully.

9
00:00:47.445 --> 00:00:50.225
"I have very strong legs.

10
00:00:51.506 --> 00:00:52.946
I can run all day long."

11
00:00:53.706 --> 00:00:56.307
The two friars looked at each other in despair.

12
00:00:56.327 --> 00:01:01.869
"I guess we have no choice," mumbled Ambrose, the tall friar.

13
00:01:01.889 --> 00:01:04.910
"Let's go!"

14
00:01:05.391 --> 00:01:06.731
Little John said brightly.

15
00:01:07.111 --> 00:01:11.453
He pushed his way between the two horses and started walking in the middle of the road.

16
00:01:11.473 --> 00:01:14.474
"I can talk to both of you while I run."

17
00:01:15.935 --> 00:01:18.336
The two friars rode slowly at first.

18
00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:24.479
They didn't want anyone to think they were being unkind by running away from another friar.

19
00:01:25.719 --> 00:01:30.186
But when they were farther from the inn, Friar Thomas, the short one, spoke up.

20
00:01:31.027 --> 00:01:34.730
"Friar Ambrose, we're traveling too slowly.

21
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.272
We need to go faster now."

22
00:01:37.292 --> 00:01:42.356
"That's right," said Little John with a pleasant smile.

23
00:01:42.376 --> 00:01:45.539
"We'll never get anywhere at this slow pace!"

24
00:01:46.259 --> 00:01:48.081
The two friars glared at him.

25
00:01:48.761 --> 00:01:53.105
Then without another word, they clucked at their horses and galloped away.

26
00:01:54.706 --> 00:01:56.768
Still, Little John kept up with them.

27
00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.301
He wasn't even breathing hard.

28
00:02:01.362 --> 00:02:04.024
But poor Friar Thomas was very fat.

29
00:02:04.744 --> 00:02:06.685
He didn't like bouncing in the saddle.

30
00:02:06.705 --> 00:02:10.267
"We have to slow down!"

31
00:02:10.728 --> 00:02:11.308
he cried.

32
00:02:11.328 --> 00:02:14.130
"What a shame," said Little John.

33
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:18.592
"But I was afraid that this fast pace would be too much for you."

34
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:25.236
Friar Thomas stayed silent, staring straight ahead and chewing on his bottom lip.

35
00:02:26.432 --> 00:02:28.294
The trio moved more slowly.

36
00:02:29.374 --> 00:02:31.336
Little John whistled while he walked.

37
00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:34.539
The two friars were silent.

38
00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.022
Soon they met three minstrels, who were all dressed in red.

39
00:02:39.603 --> 00:02:41.124
The minstrels blocked the road.

40
00:02:42.385 --> 00:02:45.167
Little John waved his staff to clear the way.

41
00:02:45.187 --> 00:02:47.109
"Make way for us!"

42
00:02:47.529 --> 00:02:48.150
he shouted.

43
00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.512
At first the minstrels just stared at the friars.

44
00:02:52.253 --> 00:02:54.495
Then they burst into loud laughter.

45
00:02:56.236 --> 00:03:00.198
They'd never seen such an unusual sight as the three friars!

46
00:03:00.858 --> 00:03:05.480
Little John laughed too, but Friar Thomas and Friar Ambrose stayed silent.

47
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.761
Soon the three of them were on their way again.

48
00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:11.223
And so it went.

49
00:03:12.523 --> 00:03:15.544
Little John laughed and joked with everyone they met.

50
00:03:16.225 --> 00:03:18.546
Friar Thomas was too embarrassed to speak.

51
00:03:19.206 --> 00:03:23.588
Friar Ambrose just stared grimly ahead, trying to think of what to do.

52
00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.205
At last they came to a crossroad and stopped.

53
00:03:27.225 --> 00:03:31.766
"Listen." Friar Ambrose glared at Little John.

54
00:03:31.786 --> 00:03:37.048
"We've had enough of your company, and we're tired of people making fun of us.

55
00:03:37.748 --> 00:03:39.789
You go your way, and we'll go ours."

56
00:03:39.809 --> 00:03:45.130
"Oh, I thought we were having a good time," said Little John.

57
00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:48.731
"But if you want me to leave, I will.

58
00:03:49.411 --> 00:03:53.970
I'm just a poor man, but I can tell by your horses that you're rich.

59
00:03:54.671 --> 00:03:59.555
Please give me a penny or two to buy bread and cheese at the next inn."

60
00:03:59.575 --> 00:04:04.139
"We don't have any money," Friar Ambrose said harshly.

61
00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:06.602
"Let's go, Friar Thomas."

62
00:04:08.543 --> 00:04:11.145
Little John caught hold of their horses' bridles.

63
00:04:11.165 --> 00:04:12.667
"Just a minute.

64
00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:16.850
If you truly have no money, we should pray about that.

65
00:04:17.451 --> 00:04:22.094
Let's kneel and ask for some money to help us continue on our journeys."

66
00:04:22.115 --> 00:04:25.957
"I'm not kneeling in the middle of the road!"

67
00:04:26.337 --> 00:04:27.598
said Friar Ambrose.

68
00:04:28.239 --> 00:04:30.940
Little John twirled his staff in a threatening manner.

69
00:04:32.321 --> 00:04:33.642
Everyone knelt in the road.

70
00:04:34.063 --> 00:04:36.845
Little John prayed loudly, asking for money.

71
00:04:36.865 --> 00:04:40.147
"Now check your pouches," said Little John.

72
00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:44.069
The friars looked inside their pouches, but there was nothing.

73
00:04:44.089 --> 00:04:48.789
"Let's try again," said Little John.

74
00:04:49.269 --> 00:04:54.213
He began praying again, asking for each friar to receive half a pound.

75
00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:56.315
"That's all the friars need.

76
00:04:56.916 --> 00:04:59.778
But please give any extra money to me."

77
00:05:00.539 --> 00:05:04.222
Little John pulled four gold coins from his own pouch.

78
00:05:04.242 --> 00:05:08.586
"Look!" He didn't say he'd had the coins all along.

79
00:05:08.606 --> 00:05:10.768
"Now you check your pouches."

80
00:05:12.004 --> 00:05:14.266
The two friars checked their pouches again.

81
00:05:14.286 --> 00:05:19.869
"Sorry. There's nothing in our pouches," said Friar Thomas.

82
00:05:19.889 --> 00:05:23.091
"Let me check," said Little John.

83
00:05:23.111 --> 00:05:25.112
"Maybe you missed something."

84
00:05:25.852 --> 00:05:27.373
And indeed they had.

85
00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:32.996
Friar Ambrose's pouch contained 110 pounds in gold coins.

86
00:05:33.657 --> 00:05:36.378
Friar Thomas's pouch held seventy pounds.

87
00:05:36.858 --> 00:05:39.380
They didn't say they'd had the coins all along.

88
00:05:40.572 --> 00:05:43.674
Little John counted out half a pound for each man.

89
00:05:43.694 --> 00:05:47.155
"And the rest of the money is mine!"

90
00:05:47.956 --> 00:05:50.017
With that, Little John left them.

91
00:05:51.277 --> 00:05:55.919
The friars looked at each other sadly, and then mounted their horses again.
